f she caught any food  like the story about the ghost being a  demon who is 10 foot tall  upon finding the last snare you see the  ocean tomoy comments on her  leaving tsushima island and sailing to  the mainland opening up an inn in kyoto  so she can greet all the beautiful  people of japan  while her servants rob them blind a  questionable goal but  nonetheless a reason to leave a war-torn  island once making it inside her house  jin knows that it's tomoy and then tomoe  confesses that the mongols withdrew her  support  but in order to help she will let jin  know the locations of where the mongols  will strike next  which is umugi cove she claims it's for  revenge but it's really so that she can  sneak away and sail for japan while the  two aren't looking you then meet up with  ishikawa and tell him the details and  then meet up with him again at umugi so  that you can go to a nearby hut and  discuss the plans with tomboy  the three travel to umuki cove so that  u3 can stop the attack they ambush the  remaining mongols and finish off those  to survive the initial ambush  and then after the fight tomoy is  nowhere to be seen jin and ishikawa  chase her down to the coast where they  find her on a boat leaving to the  mainland with a note next to her mask  the note reads sensei ishikawa we have  judged each other harshly but buddha  tells us that our greatest enemies can  be our best teachers i am grateful for  your teaching and for the chance to  fight by your side a final time  i have become your student and i would  have become your daughter but the way of  the bow is behind me now  what lies ahead i'm like an arrow shot  from a bow who knows where the wind will  take me  ishikawa is content with this and allows  her to leave and go to kyoto he tells  jin to promise him  not to make the same mistakes that he  did and that is the conclusion of  ishikawa's storyline  a stubborn master wanting to teach even  after what has happened in his past but  became too hell-bent on teaching his way  of the bow  and having an error in his lineage that  he couldn't see the darkness that  surrounded his student  but this experience has humbled him in  realizing that maybe there was some  error in his ways  and he keeps learning this throughout  the side quests that you do with him  these sidequests make him learn that  what he did was wrong and maybe he could  have gone about it a different way  but the past is the past and you must  learn from it as to not repeat the same  mistakes in the future  one thing i noticed actually was how  tomoe and ishikawa is very similar to  jin and shimra in terms of their  relationship with  tomoe and jin being the error in the  next samurai with ishikawa and shimra  being the  you know the lords and the kind of  father figure for them and also kind of  how this relationship and such  foreshadowed a little bit at the end of  the game  as ishikawa says that only a child  thinks his elders are perfect which is a  really nice reflection of ishikawa and  then also how that ties into the end of  the game with shimra  and the whole ending that happens  towards of course the end of the game i  just thought that was a really  interesting interaction that may have  been overlooked by a few people so i  thought to bring this up at the end of  the video because just for some food for  thought i want to thank you all for  joining me on this journey of ishikawa's  side quest of course let me know what  you guys think about the sciquest and  especially the video in the comments  below  expect another psyquest character next  week as usual i'm not sure who will be  tackling but that'll be surprised for  when the video goes up  but thank you for watching the video  today guys like the v if you do enjoy  subscribe if you're new  as always like i said let me know what  you thought about the side quest  ishikawa is a character  in the video in the comments below and  take care i'll see you guys next week  for another video  [